1c0j|a|Immediate; direct; close; short. ; Close-fisted; parsimonious.	j:tu5,65,3~tu5,65,3	e:1d2h,64,1~1d2h,64,1
1c0s|a|Free from that which soils, defiles, or disorders; clean; cleanly; tidy. ; Free from what is unbecoming, inappropriate, or tawdry; simple and becoming; pleasing with simplicity; tasteful; chaste; as, a neat style; a neat dress. ; Free from admixture or adulteration; good of its kind; as, neat brandy. ; Excellent in character, skill, or performance, etc.; nice; finished; adroit; as, a neat design; a neat thief. ; With all deductions or allowances made; net. [In this sense usually written net. See Net, a., 3.]	e:1lgp,64,5~1lgp,64,5
1c1k|a|Such as must be; impossible to be otherwise; not to be avoided; inevitable. ; Impossible to be otherwise, or to be dispensed with, without preventing the attainment of a desired result; indispensable; requiste; essential. ; Acting from necessity or compulsion; involuntary; -- opposed to free; as, whether man is a necessary or a free agent is a question much discussed.	j:1yak,48,4~1yak,48,4	e:1yc2,86,6;b5,64,3;1w23,56,6;1oar,35,6;1e0i,19,4~1w23,56,6;1oar,35,6;1yc2,86,6;1e0i,19,4;b5,64,3
1c3r|n|A state that requires supply or relief; pressing occasion for something; necessity; urgent want. ; Want of the means of subsistence; poverty; indigence; destitution. ; That which is needful; anything necessary to be done; (pl.) necessary things; business. ; Situation of need; peril; danger. ; To be in want of; to have cause or occasion for; to lack; to require, as supply or relief.	N:26xs,19,1~26xs,19,1
1c3r|v|To be wanted; to be necessary.	o:26xs,35,3;hi,30,3;1plj,30,5;1zml,7,7;wk2,3,1;xbo,1,6~1zml,7,7;xbo,1,6;1plj,30,5;hi,30,3;26xs,35,3;wk2,3,1	d:1c1i,39,6;b5,37,5;if0,34,9;ptd,26,5;227a,25,5;1ut3,17,6;1cdu,16,7;165x,12,7;2fi,11,7;x5,9,7~1e0i,7,18;1oar,9,11;1xx3,9,10;if0,34,9;165x,12,7;2fi,11,7;1cdu,16,7;x5,9,7;1d28,3,6;1c1i,39,6
